   "end": 3221.64,
   "pin": "moments-fresh_20261112_050611-41f29b1f",
   "text": "Bitcoin imposes a global free market for the first time ever."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "c1JGheQBPH4",
   "start": 2403.23,
   "end": 2422.07,
   "pin": "moments-fresh_20261112_050611-41f29b1f",
   "text": "I mean, the good news about Bitcoin is it's not, you know, its success is not dependent upon who's in the White House or who's controlling the Senate or the House of Representatives in the U.S. You know, price -wise, some people would say when it's when it's persecuted and when it's in the crosshairs, it tends to do pretty well."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "Sjb6lUiL0m4",
   "start": 1826.54,
   "end": 1843.48,
   "pin": "moments-fresh_20261112_050611-41f29b1f",
   "text": "However, I think Bitcoin is by far the most undervalued asset in like the entire global financial system right now. So, you know, Bitcoin gold parity is around like $1.5, $1.4 million per Bitcoin last I checked. It's very, very undervalued."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "Sjb6lUiL0m4",
   "start": 3090.75,
   "end": 3109.87,
   "pin": "moments-batch_b1_fresh_20261111_213954-1b4a63d0",
   "text": "When Bitcoin and an asset is going up and the bull market is super hot, everyone loves it. When the bear market is happening and Bitcoin is going down, everyone hates it. And like, that's why the price got high and that's why the price got low, because everyone loved it at the top and everyone wanted exposure and everyone hated it and didn't want exposure at the bottom."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "vgsSZ4mAHfQ",
   "start": 4664.57,
   "end": 4673.21,
   "pin": "moments-batch_b1_fresh_20261111_213954-1b4a63d0",
   "text": "Bitcoin shows you that you can just increase the purchasing power. So the value of Bitcoin goes up without the supply of Bitcoin going up. So the people who hold Bitcoin don't get robbed."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "UJFQBaMh3yg",
   "start": 191.38,
   "end": 203.06,
   "pin": "moments-batch_b1_fresh_20261111_213954-1b4a63d0",
   "text": "Now, higher rates make cash more attractive and borrowed money more expensive, which is very much the wrong combo for anything risky, and the market definitely sees Bitcoin as risky."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "BS0XC_tixa8",
   "start": 994.329,
   "end": 1005.909,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_073738-d2657bbe",
   "text": "Bitcoin is the one piece of open source technology that can't be shut down, silenced or removed. If Bitcoin wins, open source wins. And every stat you hold is a vote against the digital prison being built around all of us."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "WTCwyxW-lHk",
   "start": 1685.968,
   "end": 1695.698,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_073738-d2657bbe",
   "text": "But we have very rarely in Bitcoin's history seen six negative weeks back to back to back to back to back. to back. I think that was six."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "mJviDNOhIyw",
   "start": 1614.601,
   "end": 1630.831,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_073738-d2657bbe",
   "text": "But then if someone doesn't understand Bitcoin and you drop... 25 % of their portfolio in Bitcoin and Bitcoin goes down 50%. You get fired and they sell their Bitcoin. And so that is, I think, why you've seen people like BlackRock, I think, logically walk that back to one, five percent allocation."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "DcUbBkyeh9M",
   "start": 236.688,
   "end": 253.308,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_183302-0c68b589",
   "text": "A CEO makes a personal mistake in shareholders pay. A government mismanages its currencies. and its savers pay. Bitcoin's rules aren't kept by a single executive or a single central bank. They're enforced by thousands of independent computers running the same code. No CEO, no compromise, no committee to debate."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "GXWj2JO9bz8",
   "start": 124.157,
   "end": 138.097,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_183302-0c68b589",
   "text": "I don't really think Bitcoin and crypto are partisan issues, right? Bitcoin and crypto are about how do we modernize the financial markets and how we would create financial freedom for 350 Americans and 8 billion people around the world."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "mKNAcOFMYD4",
   "start": 755.454,
   "end": 764.214,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_183302-0c68b589",
   "text": "My biggest fear is that I go to the bank and I punch in my code and the money's not there because the bank owns the money and they could just take it from me. And that's why that's why we Bitcoin."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "DcUbBkyeh9M",
   "start": 216.054,
   "end": 228.674,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_215708-13949b7c",
   "text": "Currencies are often born for political reasons, but fail for economic reasons. Bitcoin launched in January of 2009. It's never been renamed. It's never gone into another currency. It's never been redenominated or reissued."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "MqVqfEDXgLo",
   "start": 937.971,
   "end": 957.291,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_215708-13949b7c",
   "text": "I think, well, what we've seen in the market is on Thursday, Friday, there was actually a much bigger drop in traditional stock prices, especially tech stock. There's like 10, 20%, like Intel dropped 29%. Whereas Bitcoin only dropped like five, six percent."
  },
  {
   "video_id": "HWuMai_mAug",
   "start": 1691.139,
   "end": 1698.069,
   "pin": "moments-ledger_20261113_215708-13949b7c",
   "text": "I think treasury companies will also bleed to Bitcoin. I mean, basically, everything in the industry eventually bleeds to Bitcoin."
  }
